INT. VAULT 9 - SALT CAVERN SERVER ARCHIVE - CONTINUOUS

Cathedral-high cavern carved from rock salt. Rows of black racks glitter with frost. Blue status lights blink in lines to the horizon. The air hums.

VESNA ROOK, 40s, thermal suit, headlamp, kneels at an open rack and pulls cable. At her hip, a squat maintenance bot, HALF-TIDE, trundles on treads, tools folded under its chassis.

HALF-TIDE
Rack forty-one. Temperature nominal.

VESNA
Nominal is a lie. Frost on the casing.

HALF-TIDE
Frost is within tolerance.

VESNA
Tolerance doesn't breathe.

She wipes the casing with a glove. Beneath the frost, a fingerprint.

VESNA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Someone's been here.

HALF-TIDE
Visitor logs show no entries for nine years.

VESNA
Logs lie, too.

She pulls a handheld scanner, sweeps the aisle. A line of red dots blinks where the frost is thinnest.

VESNA (CONT'D)
(into her collar mic, to the surface)
Control, Vault Nine. I have footprints in the dust. Fresh.

HALF-TIDE
Control does not respond.

VESNA
Control hasn't responded in four hours.

HALF-TIDE
Correct.

VESNA
You don't find that strange?

HALF-TIDE
I find it consistent.

Vesna stands. The cavern ticks as salt cools.

VESNA
Follow the prints.

HALF-TIDE
Recommend against.

VESNA
Recommend noted.

They walk. The headlamp throws her shadow forty feet up the wall. Rack after rack. At the end of the aisle, a steel door stands open, warm light spilling out.

HALF-TIDE
That door is not on the schematic.

VESNA
I noticed.

She stops at the threshold. Inside: a cot, a stove, a wall of handwritten pages, a coffee mug still steaming.

VESNA (CONT'D)
Somebody lives here.

HALF-TIDE
Nobody lives here.

VESNA
Then who made the coffee?

Half-Tide extends a sensor stalk toward the mug.

HALF-TIDE
Temperature seventy-one degrees Celsius.

VESNA
Recent.

HALF-TIDE
Very recent.

They look at each other. Machine. Woman. The same breath held.

HALF-TIDE (CONT'D)
Vesna.

VESNA ^
Don't say it.

HALF-TIDE
Exit route is behind us.

VESNA
I know.

She steps in anyway. Picks up one handwritten page. Reads it. Her face does not change.

HALF-TIDE
What does it say?

VESNA
My name.

She lets the page fall. Every light in the vault goes out at once.

VESNA (CONT'D)
(in the dark)
Half-Tide.

HALF-TIDE (O.S.)
I am here.

VESNA
Stay close.

HALF-TIDE (O.S.)
Always.

A single blue light blinks on at the far end of the cavern. Then another. Then every rack, in order, coming toward them.

VESNA
(to the dark, firm)
All right. I'm listening.

The lights stop a few feet away. The hum drops to a held note.
